gametitle=Madden NFL 2004 (SLUS-20752) [14F8B841]
comment=P11 -- one word: stop the helper re-arming the doubled defender's shed-lock. Over P1+P4.
// Lane 3's key contrast, made testable in a single word. On slot 9 the C/NT
// and LG pairs DO reach native driven-back outcomes (shed ids 121 and 129).
// The double team never can, because its own kind-8 helper re-arms the
// doubled defender's shed-lock +0x42C := 16 at every lapse (0x001f21e4/e8).
// TryShedMove (0x001a7130) is gated on that lock being 0, so the doubled man
// is the ONE defender on the field who never gets to contest -- and the
// engine's driven-back/pancake vocabulary lives only on the LOSING side of
// that contest (lose chains 0x00526668 run / 0x00526710 pass -> ids 120-131).
//
// 0x001F21E8: addiu a1, zero, 16 -> addiu a1, zero, 0. The lock is set to
// zero instead of 16, so the shed contest may run for a doubled defender.
// Against two blockers he should LOSE it, which is the native drive.
//
// This is the cheapest possible test of lane 3's whole thesis, and it beats
// N-1 (a ~55-word cave) as the FIRST move because a null here refutes the
// thesis before that cave is written. Risk: he may WIN the shed and beat the
// double team -- which would be a different and informative failure.
// Position-writing caves are removed; P8/P9/P10 are all superseded.

